.TH NIX\-SCOUT 1 "August 2026" "nix\-scout 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nix\-scout \- scout module switcher for NixOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nix\-scout
.I command
.RI [ argument ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nix\-scout
materializes, builds, and applies scout modules \(em subflakes under a configured
modules directory that each export a
.B .#scout
output.
Each module is an isolated Nix flake that installs programs into a dedicated
per\-user profile or copies home\-files into
.IR $HOME ,
without requiring a full
.BR nixos\-rebuild (8).
.PP
The parent flake\(aqs
.I flake.lock
is stamped into each materialized module so all inputs are pinned consistently.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List available scout modules found under
.IR $NIX_SCOUT_MODULES .
Each entry is a directory containing a
.IR flake.nix .
.TP
.BI switch " name"
Materialize the named module to a temporary directory, build its
.B packages.<system>.scout
output, and apply it.
If the output contains a
.I bin/
directory the result is installed into the scout profile via
.BR nix\-env (1)
and a Fish
.I conf.d
snippet is written so the profile is on
.B PATH
in new sessions.
If the output contains a
.I home\-files/
directory its contents are copied into
.IR $HOME .
.TP
.BI switch " path"
Install a store path
.RI ( /nix/store/\&... )
or flake installable
.RI ( ref # attr )
directly into the scout profile without materializing or building a module.
.TP
.B status
Show the active scout profile path, installed programs, and each registered
gc\-root with its resolved store path.
.TP
.B clear
Uninstall all packages from the scout profile, remove gc\-root symlinks, and
delete the Fish
.I conf.d
snippet.
.TP
.BR help | \-\-help | \-h
Print usage information.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NIX_SCOUT_MODULES
Path to the directory containing scout module subflakes.
Baked in at build time via
.B @scoutModules@
substitution; can be overridden at runtime with this variable.
.TP
.B NIX_SCOUT_PARENT
Path to the parent flake root.
Its
.I flake.lock
is copied into each materialized module so inputs are pinned to the same
revisions as the parent.
Baked in at build time via
.B @scoutParent@
substitution.
.TP
.B NIX_SCOUT_PROFILE
Full path to the per\-user Nix profile.
Defaults to
.IR /nix/var/nix/profiles/per\-user/$USER/nix\-scout .
.TP
.B NIX_SCOUT_GCROOTS
Full path to the per\-user gc\-roots directory.
Defaults to
.IR /nix/var/nix/gcroots/per\-user/$USER/nix\-scout .
.SH SUDO MODE
.B sudo nix\-scout
is supported.
When run as root,
.B nix\-scout
reads
.B SUDO_USER
and resolves the real invoker\(aqs profile paths and
.B HOME
from
.IR /etc/passwd ,
so all paths remain correct and no secondary
.BR sudo (8)
calls are needed for directory or symlink operations.
Direct invocation as root without
.B SUDO_USER
set is rejected.
.SH SCOUT MODULES
A scout module is a directory under
.I $NIX_SCOUT_MODULES
containing a
.I flake.nix
that exports
.BR packages.<system>.scout .
The output must be one of:
.IP \(bu 2
A derivation with a
.I bin/
subdirectory \(em installed into the scout profile via
.BR nix\-env (1).
.IP \(bu 2
A derivation with a
.I home\-files/
subdirectory \(em each file is copied verbatim into
.IR $HOME ,
preserving the relative path structure.
.PP
Scout modules cannot set system\-wide NixOS options.
Use the core flake or
.B nixos\-rebuild
for that.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /nix/var/nix/profiles/per\-user/$USER/nix\-scout
The dedicated scout Nix profile.
.TP
.I /nix/var/nix/gcroots/per\-user/$USER/nix\-scout/
Directory of gc\-root symlinks preventing installed store paths from being
garbage collected.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fish/conf.d/nix\-scout.fish
Written after a successful profile\-mode install so the scout profile bin is on
.B PATH
in new Fish sessions.
Removed by
.BR "nix\-scout clear" .
Do not edit manually.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error, module not found, or build failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nix\-env (1),
.BR nix (1),
.BR nixos\-rebuild (8)
